  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0400 and it contains six tables. The first table is Role, which has three columns: Permission_Description, Role_ID, and Role_Name. The Role_ID column is the primary key and the Role_Name column is a string. The second table is Book, which has six columns: Author, Book_Category, Book_ID, Book_Name, Publication_Date, and Publisher. The Book_ID column is the primary key and the Book_Name column is a string. The third table is User, which has eight columns: College, Email, Password, Registration_Time, Role_ID, User_ID, Username, and FOREIGN KEY (Role_ID) REFERENCES Role(Role_ID). The Role_ID column is not null and the User_ID column is the primary key. The fourth table is Notification, which has five columns: Notification_Content, Notification_ID, Notification_Title, Publisher_ID, and Release_Date. The Notification_ID column is the primary key and the Publisher_ID column is a foreign key that references the User table. The fifth table is User_Establishes_Friend_Relationship, which has four columns: Creation_Time, Friend_ID, User_ID, and PRIMARY KEY (User_ID, Friend_ID). The Friend_ID column is a foreign key that references the User table and the User_ID column is a foreign key that references the User table. The sixth table is User_Borrows_Book, which has five columns: Book_ID, Borrow_Time, Return_Time, User_ID, and PRIMARY KEY (User_ID, Book_ID). The Book_ID column is a foreign key that references the Book table and the User_ID column is a foreign key that references the User table.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirement Description:\nThis is an online instant messaging service platform system. In terms of role management, the system supports the management of different user roles such as students, teachers, and colleges, each with its corresponding role name and permission settings. In user management, the system records each user’s basic information, including a unique User ID, Username, Password, College, Email, and Registration Time, while also assigning the appropriate role to each user. In book management, the system maintains book information, including Book ID, Book Name, Author, Publisher, Publication Date, and Book Category, and supports users borrowing multiple books. In notification management, the system supports users in publishing and managing notification information. Each notification includes Notification ID, Notification Title, Notification Content, Publisher ID, and Release Date. All users can serve as the publisher of notifications.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0400.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0400\nCREATE TABLE `role` (\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `role_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `permission_description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`role_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `book_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `author` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `book_category` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `publication_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `publisher` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `college` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `registration_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `role` (`role_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `notification` (\n  `notification_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `notification_title` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `notification_content` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `publisher_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `release_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`notification_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `notification_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`publisher_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_establishes_friend_relationship` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `friend_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `friend_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_establishes_friend_relationship_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_establishes_friend_relationship_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`friend_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_borrows_book` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `borrow_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `return_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `book_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_borrows_book_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_borrows_book_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
